<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09544efd2542bf73d6c82607cdabb066409ff95f02ff1f4ce8f66a37dcca2ad2</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the growing debt burden, and will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3ad7174fb4b2320b84652d9e57a7f5428bfc1cf43daa6f1b9472cf6d4d95cd7</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: 'Woman, Life, Freedom' lives on despite war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f15c3d63f372f468f90fdec511fa7c1cdc2ed9089dd2395b9b8151495af339d</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-woman-life-freedom-lives-on-despite-war/a-79276123--cc6a8d951841.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-woman-life-freedom-lives-on-despite-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Jina Mahsa Amini triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bangladesh court sentences 7 Hasina allies to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fc3bef5751f24fcf2e035ff5d975e175231db7319f2950642905495c6c5c92a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131--93bfc83fec03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest verdict brings to 22 the number of death sentences handed down in cases stemming from the 2024 uprising that ended Sheikh Hasina's 15-year rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin election driven by radical ideas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33d6f526fba83934cd0e50dd67b63064b6f30f61e27ede7f2b18a80caecc8dcd</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516--15d2b53f017a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The results of the Berlin election are as hard to predict as ever. Three parties are vying for first place, including the socialist Left Party and the far-right AfD. But one issue is most important to Berliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police find arms depot near highway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff81a66dc2c581968db2f62a1e7668e11b722fdcdcbbed481fe89e616c30d619</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-find-arms-depot-near-highway/live-79273324--57b471e5aa19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-find-arms-depot-near-highway/live-79273324?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have found a stash of rifles, pistols and other firearms near a road in the western state of Rhineland-Palatinate. Meanwhile, Defense Minister Pistorius is off to Washington for talks with his US counterpart.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SPD governor campaigns as one-woman bulwark against AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:462104044b459afba1119c68863744c482e0f005f81f3e29bac3b5762dd791b7</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225--0135376188de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuela Schwesig, of the center-left SPD, has governed the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, on the Baltic Sea coast, since 2017. Ahead of this weekend's election, she is campaigning against the nationalist AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US confirms it has weapons in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efdc6464653a637283083f937c68e9f4f10503461b316f54ba58331fcceffb5b</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894--7b3b13289f4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force justified the weapons deployment by citing its two biggest geopolitical rivals — Russia and China. Beijing responded by urging Washington to "stop preparing for war" in outer space.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NATO jets shoot down drone over Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfe393535300e2605e198453f450bbc03c104cd2e81d89ec0855a77fffc34bf</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975--4d3ef910416c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drone, which is believed to have entered Lithuanian airspace from Belarus, was shot down by an Italian fighter jet in between the cities of Vilnius and Kaunas. There have been no reports of casualties or damage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian warship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b7c23ceac18c308699abe6b89f116e62d55a8c69463e8bb6a123ee49fbf55b0</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510--158a6506bc4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denmark has summoned Russia's ambassador over a Baltic Sea encounter that Copenhagen says is part of an increasingly aggressive pattern of Russian behavior.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China tightens travel rules over tech security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6770010b4dfa0b4b0d6d576e453d5aba33c737ef4b225e25da80ea5186bc12fc</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-tightens-travel-rules-over-tech-security/a-79270217--ad2e766020cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-tightens-travel-rules-over-tech-security/a-79270217?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says the new rules, which could also apply to foreign and Taiwanese nationals, are aimed at safeguarding "national security."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d644b4b2a38a713134b2c5abaab2589d548ff6ed7335347031cf6c9bd6fd4c6c</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Meta to report child abuse cases to law enforcement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93fa0711ca878244b4cddcb8c84ad705333c11559a5a352917763b839ef87a65</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-meta-to-report-child-abuse-cases-to-law-enforcement/live-79268751--04c495e204f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-meta-to-report-child-abuse-cases-to-law-enforcement/live-79268751?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tech giant Meta will now directly report child safety-related cases to India's cybercrime portal, according to media reports. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why top AI researchers are warning about human extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce9944a121878fea57d304aa5eaf5026bacca28e8eb6fdc61d1466a1abbb4a8</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-top-ai-researchers-are-warning-about-human-extinction/a-79263146--1de1f181920f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-top-ai-researchers-are-warning-about-human-extinction/a-79263146?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence pose an existential threat to humanity? Some leading researchers are warning against an unregulated race toward AI superintelligence.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador court hands down first life sentence for femicide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bffb9ee30003164fee3f787b23c75c803d98076ee682939ca7c98c5b72946ef</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-salvador-court-hands-down-first-life-sentence-for-femicide/a-79268746--3332ccb66681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-salvador-court-hands-down-first-life-sentence-for-femicide/a-79268746?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The landmark conviction comes 42 days after the killing of a woman in Santa Ana who prosecutors said was stalked and harassed by her neighbor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US: Two countries and the pistachio between them</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a658938a9256f13844790ff5411d2e90741f9f43329ca61a2395796fdd6c51fb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310--28756f33fc8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pistachios sold across the United States have a surprising history: California's trees trace their roots to Iran. Now, both regions face the same threat — their farmland is sinking as groundwater disappears.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caa6534b2c115f2510e909c11d8c154f53407a8463602fd60abff032afdbecc4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US scraps greenhouse gas rules for power plants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a89c72dc5e5e61dc454ea9fcb321c227aafc23dc5f2193bee6cdbbd3863563c0</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T05:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-scraps-greenhouse-gas-rules-for-power-plants/a-79268393--51c0df356c7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-scraps-greenhouse-gas-rules-for-power-plants/a-79268393?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Environmental Protection Agency said it was repealing Biden-era limits on emissions made by power plants, in the "largest power sector deregulation action ever."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court denies Trump bid to restrict mail-in ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1680c47f8f078c621ca267a7fdeeab9b67d03f2a5e0b7660eb6769b203af3f5</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-supreme-court-denies-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-in-ballots/a-79267854--d0b3a2fd6f50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-supreme-court-denies-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-in-ballots/a-79267854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The court said election officials do not have sufficient time to implement the rule before the November midterms. Trump has argued, without providing evidence, that the system is vulnerable to fraud.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz urges CDU discipline as pressure grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03164249d606e059901df34c1285f6330a5018addf08c529f398782d09c316e9</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902--10c6578e951f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has urged his party to stay disciplined as pressure grows over his leadership. Meanwhile, Germany's homeownership rate has fallen to its lowest level in 20 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kremlin-linked Russian oligarch helped fund Trump Jr.'s wedding celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e921b4cd3ed6425b5a3ecb28e4aab13e91b6417b975ca02986ccb592ee85d78</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kremlin-linked-russian-oligarch-helped-fund-trump-jr-s-wedding-celebration/a-79267341--78068d8783fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kremlin-linked-russian-oligarch-helped-fund-trump-jr-s-wedding-celebration/a-79267341?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump's son and his wife confirmed reports that Umar Kremlev paid for parts of the festivities. Kremlev was awarded the "Order of Friendship" by Putin earlier this year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
